            "\n",
            "\\textbf{Least-to-most prompting.} Like the last-letter-concatenation task in Section \\ref{sec:symbolic_manipulation}, least-to-most prompting for SCAN is based on two kinds of prompts: (1) a command decomposition prompt containing 8 exemplars to demonstrate how to decompose a long command to a list of short commands (see Table~\\ref{table: scan-reducing} for some of these exemplars);  and (2) a command mapping prompt containing 14 exemplars to demonstrate how to map natural language commands to action sequences (see Table~\\ref{table: scan-mapping} for some of these exemplars). The full prompt contexts for both decomposition and mapping are listed in Appendix~\\ref{app:scan}. The exemplars used in the command-mapping prompt are intended to fully cover the semantics of the SCAN commands.  \n",
