            "\\textbf{Results}. We compare least-to-most prompting with chain-of-thought prompting and standard few-shot prompting. The exemplars for standard few-shot prompting are derived from the chain-of-thought prompt by removing the intermediate explanations.  The accuracies of different prompting methods with different language models are presented in Table~\\ref{table: scan-results}. Example outputs can be found in Appendix~\\ref{app:scan-outputs}. Using \\texttt{code-davinci-002}, least-to-most prompting achieves an accuracy of $99.7\\\n",
            " We also test least-to-most prompting on all other splits and even the full SCAN dataset. We find that its solving rate remains the same. In addition, it may be interesting to note that \\texttt{code-davinci-002} consistently outperforms \\texttt{text-davinci-002}, regardless of the prompting method.  \n",
